(text "SIROKKO 262.01 - INTEGRATED MINIMAL SAFETY / DRAFT\nYD-ESP32-S3 N16R8; native hierarchical schematic candidate.\nDRAFT / NOT FOR ORDER / NO POWER / NO FIRE. PCB and firmware not yet synchronized."
	(at 25.4 25.4 0)
	(effects
		(font
			(size 1.27 1.27)
		)
		
	 (justify left top))
	(uuid "f1705f73-79aa-4f8d-8ed6-9f68bf3391e7")
)
(text "ON-BOARD TEMPERATURE INTERFACES\nU9/U10 are MAX31856 for the two K-type thermocouples.\nJ12: 1=3V3, 2=DS18B20 DQ, 3=GND.\nProbe wiring, cold-junction error and fault thresholds still require verification."
	(at 25.4 42.672 0)
	(effects
		(font
			(size 1.27 1.27)
		)
		
	 (justify left top))
	(uuid "798c3819-deea-418d-a655-a27ceac4b24e")
)
(text "ON-BOARD RELAY AND SAFETY STAGES\nMinimalSafety controls U11 DRV8803 and K1/K2/K3 coil sinks.\nGLOW_CMD and FUEL_CMD are separate; nENBL is the common hardware inhibit.\nMotor PWM/purge remains separate. Switched contact and power ratings remain unqualified."
	(at 142.24 137.16 0)
	(effects
		(font
			(size 1.27 1.27)
		)
		
	 (justify left top))
	(uuid "a32d2430-92f6-4b14-b073-bf061508d25a")
)
(text "MAIN INPUT / ROOM SENSOR\nJ13: 1=VIN_RAW_24, 2=GND. Main design range 21.6..28.8V.\n5V conversion is on-board; USB/external power arbitration remains unqualified.\nJ12: 1=3V3, 2=DQ, 3=GND. Never connect raw 24V to logic terminals."
	(at 25.4 175.26 0)
	(effects
		(font
			(size 1.27 1.27)
		)
		
	 (justify left top))
	(uuid "a26a683b-7ac9-4a62-9c63-46d72f52b918")
)
(text "DEFINED INPUTS / OUTPUTS\nR1: room-sensor pull-up; R2/R3: thermocouple CS pull-ups.\nR7/R8: fan/PWM pulldowns. Safety pull resistors are inside MinimalSafety.\nGPIO21 MCU_PERMIT and GPIO41 ARM_PULSE are outputs; GPIO6 P24_PRESENT is INPUT ONLY.\nGPIO8 = TFT_DC; GPIO48 remains for the DevKit RGB LED. No RGB jumper removal.\nGPIO42 / former SW_TRIP is unconnected. New firmware only after PCB completion."
	(at 25.4 269.24 0)
	(effects
		(font
			(size 1.27 1.27)
		)
		
	 (justify left top))
	(uuid "5da8c089-5e3e-4b0a-bcf2-bfc0b44e5dce")
)
(text "MINIMUM HARDWARE PERMISSION - DRAFT\nU1 watchdog; U2 asynchronous-clear latch; U6 three AND gates. U11 is the coil driver.\nU20 P24 presence monitor retained: USB can keep ESP32 alive during main-power loss.\nReturn of any permission does not itself re-arm the latch; require a fresh ARM_PULSE.\nThe majority of process protections belongs to the ESP32 state machine, not extra logic ICs."
	(at 210.82 254.0 0)
	(effects
		(font
			(size 1.27 1.27)
		)
	 (justify left top))
	(uuid "0efdce91-6b1b-4bc4-9ca6-cddffc2f92e4")
)
(text "J24 RESET ACTUAL PIN CONTRACT (NKK BB25AB-FA)\n1=EN_CHIP_PU NO; 2=GND COM; 3=unused NC. Hardware RESET grounds DevKit EN.\n4=unused NO; 5=3V3 COM; 6=RESET_RELEASED NC, pulled LOW by R702 when open.\nJ25 REMOVED: no external power or permit interface.\nTemperature conditions belong to MCU_PERMIT, asserted only by the qualified control cycle.\nU6.1 and U6.2 both receive WD_OK; no permanently asserted new input. R701 removed. Reset timing is unqualified."
	(at 25.4 375.92 0)
	(effects
		(font
			(size 1.27 1.27)
		)
	 (justify left top))
	(uuid "ffac4b6b-0c63-418a-89b3-ece37d5ecc0e")
)
(text "DRAFT: LM5013 5V is assigned to +5V_DEVKIT in this hierarchy. USB reverse-feed arbitration remains UNQUALIFIED. NO POWER."
	(at 430 35 0)
	(effects
		(font
			(size 1.27 1.27)
		)
	 (justify left top))
	(uuid "33efe872-0624-43e1-a6dd-3bb54058eb20")
)
(text "J27 GLOW: 1=switched positive; 2=power GND.\nSchematic assigned; PCB current/transient qualification OPEN. NO POWER / NO FIRE."
	(at 25.4 320.04 0)
	(effects
		(font
			(size 1.27 1.27)
		)
	 (justify left top))
	(uuid "ac24e33c-f203-43d5-9433-4ef406c30914")
)
(text "J28 CLUTCH: 1=switched positive; 2=power GND.\nSchematic assigned; PCB current/transient qualification OPEN. NO POWER / NO FIRE."
	(at 25.4 335.28 0)
	(effects
		(font
			(size 1.27 1.27)
		)
	 (justify left top))
	(uuid "520582ff-6e87-42ea-aea6-55c4951d1894")
)
(text "RELAY DRIVER DRAFT / NO POWER / NO FIRE\nU11 DRV8803PWPR: nENBL=HIGH disables all sinks.\nU2 Q -> SAFETY_OK -> U11 IN3. U2 /Q -> RELAY_DISABLE -> U11 nENBL.\nGLOW_CMD -> U11 IN1; FUEL_CMD -> U11 IN2; commands remain separate.\nC21=100nF/100V; C22=330uF/63V. Driver limits, coil release, transient and thermal tests pending.\nThe former U12/U14 gating and C23/C26 bypasses are removed, not silently bypassed."
	(at 330.2 233.68 0)
	(effects
		(font
			(size 1.27 1.27)
		)
	 (justify left top))
	(uuid "c6122bfe-2256-4882-8660-903a9cd09c0b")
)
